 "description": "Use this when the user wants to test an app idea with TikTok slideshows before coding, such as \"make 4 slideshows for this idea\". Pass idea, and angles 3 or 4 (default 4). Returns that many angles. Each angle has 5 slides (hook, pain, stake, reveal, cta), each a 1080x1920 PNG in png_base64, plus one caption and a hashtag list. Quote the summary field first. It has the counts and the first caption. Save png_base64 as its filename only when the user asks for the files. Stake is the second pain beat. The story reveal listens for the comment what is the app. One call is one plugin-call. The same page is at /slides. It does not publish or store the idea.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "angles": {
    "description": "How many angles to make. Default 4. Each angle is 5 slides.",
    "maximum": 4,
    "minimum": 3,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "idea": {
    "description": "The app or startup idea to test. Slides use only this text plus fixed angle frames. Do not include secrets.",
    "maxLength": 280,
    "minLength": 8,
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "idea"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
 "name": "draft_tiktok_slides",
